There are many open-source LLMs (large Language Models) -> OpenAI, Gemini, Groq etc.


i/p ---> LLM ---> o/p => Simple GenAI application flow.


But LLM can't provide current information/ recent info due to cut-off training data. 
Hence it needs to rely on some third party tool to get current info. 
Ex: Current stock price, weather info etc.


i/p ---> LLM ---> Tool (which returns context back to LLM) ---> LLM ---> o/p => Basic Agent Architecture.

Langchain made easy to build an Agent. Before this, we were using ReAct Architecture.

Practice -> langchain-practice\1-langchainintro.ipynb

How does the LLM know which tool to call for which user query? The doc-string and name of the tool is sent to the LLM along with the user query. LLM reads them and decides which tool to call.

